": true}, {"id": "C08", "raw": "The fault code that is typically raised when the drive current of an AX-731 drive exceeds 24 amperes would depend on the specific model and manufacturer's specifications. However, a common fault code for overcurrent conditions in many drives is \"OC\" or \"Over Current.\" \n\nFor the AX-731 drive, you should refer to the manufacturer's manual or documentation to find the exact fault code. If the manual is not available, you can usually find this information in the fault code section of the drive's user manual or technical documentation.\n\nIf you have the manual, look for a section that lists fault codes and their meanings, and search for the code associated with overcurrent conditions. If you don't have the manual, you can also contact the manufacturer's technical support for assistance.", "hit": false}, {"id": "C09", "raw": "For the AX-731 fault F17, the required reset procedure typically involves the following steps:\n\n1. **Power Down the Device**: Turn off the power supply to the AX-731 device.\n2. **Wait for a Few Minutes**: Allow the device to cool down and reset internally. This usually takes about 5-10 minutes.\n3. **Check Connections**: Ensure all connections, including power and signal lines, are secure and properly connected.\n4. **Power Up the Device**: Turn the power back on and observe if the fault persists.\n5. **Clear Fault Code**: If the device has a user interface, follow the manufacturer's instructions to clear the fault code. This might involve pressing specific buttons or navigating through a menu.\n6. **Run Diagnostic Tests**: If the fault code is cleared, run any diagnostic tests recommended by the manufacturer to ensure the device is functioning correctly.\n7. **Consult Documentation**: If the", "hit": false}]
